      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "First project-side consumption of the fuzzed configuration prefix. `flb_parser_create()` sees `format == \"logfmt\"` and stores `FLB_PARSER_LOGFMT` in the parser object, which later makes `flb_parser_do()` route the payload into `logfmt_parser()`."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_strptime_arg_must_use_safe_tmp_copy",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "src/flb_parser.c",
      "function": "flb_parser_time_lookup",
      "line": 765,
      "operands": [
        "time_ptr",
        "tmp"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "time_ptr",
        "right": "tmp"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_strptime_arg_must_use_safe_tmp_copy",
      "fine_trace_step": 9,
      "description": "Root cause. After parser creation set `parser->time_with_year = FLB_TRUE`, the else-path in `flb_parser_time_lookup()` leaves `time_ptr` aliased to the bounded six-byte slice `80446.` and forwards it directly to `flb_strptime()` even though logfmt values are not NUL-terminated C strings. The fix adds the missing temporary copy and explicit terminator immediately before this call."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_conv_num_dereferences_day_cursor",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "src/flb_strptime.c",
      "function": "_conv_num",
      "line": 674,
      "operands": [
        "*buf",
        "bp"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "*buf",
        "right": "bp"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_day_parse_cursor_reaches_conv_num_sink",
      "fine_trace_step": 13,
      "description": "ASan crash site. `_conv_num()`'s first digit test dereferences the byte immediately beyond the caller's six-byte time slice while trying to parse the `%d` field that does not exist."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_day_parse_cursor_is_slice_end",
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_slice_end_reaches_day_parse_cursor",
      "role": "intermediate",
      "file": "src/flb_strptime.c",
      "function": "_flb_strptime",
      "line": 314,
      "fine_trace_step": 12,
      "state": "At the `%d` branch, `_flb_strptime()` calls `_conv_num(&bp, ...)` with `bp` already equal to the end pointer of the string previously handed to `flb_strptime()`, i.e. the parser has consumed `%s.` and is now positioned exactly at the slice boundary.",
      "operands": [
